## std.mem — heap allocation primitives (docs/manual/20-memory.md).
##
## `alloc(N)` returns a heap-allocated byte slice backed by the
## always-emitted `__zag_page_alloc` preamble helper
## (src/codegen/core.zig → std.heap.page_allocator). The caller MUST
## free with the `free` keyword (`defer free(buf)`), which emits the
## matching `std.heap.page_allocator.free(buf)` for slice targets —
## same allocator, so the ownership contract is unchanged from the
## pre-migration shape.
##
## v0.1 Tier-1 migration: the pre-migration `builtin_alloc` router
## row emitted `(std.heap.page_allocator.alloc(u8, N) catch
## @panic("OOM"))` inline. Retired — this real .zag body is the
## single source of truth. Callers must now `import std.mem.{alloc}`
## (the bare-name router no longer rewrites the call site).

pub fun alloc(n: usize) -> []u8 {
    let p: *raw u8 = __zag_page_alloc(n);
    return p[0..n];
}
